title: The TV Debate Challenge
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/tv_debate.jpg
tags: campaign
view-if: tv_debate_decided = 0
on-arrival: tv_debate_decided = 1; month_actions += 1

= The TV Debate Challenge

London Weekend Television offers to stage a televised debate between the party leaders. [+ lab_leader +] has accepted at once, and thinks he would win.

- @accept: Accept the debate.
- @decline: Decline: this election is about policies, not personalities.

@accept
on-arrival: {!
var chance = 40 + (Q.thatcher_rating - Q.lab_leader_rating) + 2 * Q.strike_wave;
if (chance < 15) {
    chance = 15;
} else if (chance > 85) {
    chance = 85;
}
Q.debate_win = (Math.random() * 100 < chance) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: accept_win if debate_win = 1; accept_lose if debate_win = 0

@accept_win
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 6; lab_leader_rating -= 4; c1_con += 3*(1-dissent); c2_con += 3*(1-dissent)
achievement: debate_win

[+ lab_leader +] plays to the gallery; you have the figures. Afterwards, the snap polls give it to you.

@accept_lose
on-arrival: thatcher_rating -= 5; lab_leader_rating += 3; c1_con -= 2; c2_con -= 2

You come across as shrill and [+ lab_leader +] as reassuring. Central Office spends the next morning on damage control.

@decline
on-arrival: thatcher_rating -= 1

You say the election is about policies, not personalities. Labour calls you frightened of the debate, but the story fades within a day.
